    {
      "title": "France imposes partial curfews in several cities, including parts of Paris",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/french-police-lost-control-during-riots-concedes-interior-minister",
      "description": "<p>Interior minister concedes police ‘lost control’ of weekend protests as PM vows to restore public order</p><p>Partial curfews have been issued for a number of French cities, including parts of Paris, after the government admitted police had “lost control” during violent weekend protests around the country.</p><p>Sébastien Lecornu, the French prime minister, said after an emergency cabinet meeting on Monday he was “fully resolved to restore public order” and had called for “local and partial” curfews if needed. There was “no question” of imposing a full curfew on entire cities, he said.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/french-police-lost-control-during-riots-concedes-interior-minister\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-19T18:16:45"
    },
    {
      "title": "France Imposes Curfews in Parts of Paris and Other Cities After Nationwide Rioting",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/19/world/europe/france-protests-riots.html",
      "description": "The interior minister acknowledged that the police were underprepared for the scale of the riots. But Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu defended their efforts and pledged to restore order.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-19T19:25:50"
    }
